---
import Shot from '../Shot.astro';

// The app's own cards, cut from its captures at the card's edges (crops of scripts/screenshots/capture.sh's frames,
// light and dark; see the README), so each sits on the page as a piece of the interface rather than a screenshot in
// a box. The CSV shows five of DayExport.header's 40 columns, in its order; a planned meal leaves the eaten columns
// empty, because a plan is never reported as eaten.
const csv = [
  ['Meal', 'Food', 'Eaten (g)', 'Eaten calories (kcal)', 'Planned (g)'],
  ['Lunch', 'Chicken breast, roasted', '180', '281', '150'],
  ['Lunch', 'Brown rice, cooked', '180', '220', '180'],
  ['Dinner', 'Salmon, baked', '', '', '165'],
];
---
<section class="week wrap" aria-labelledby="week-title">
  <div class="frame week__in">
    <h2 id="week-title" class="head" data-reveal>A week with Residual</h2>

    <div class="stage" data-reveal>
      <p><strong>On Sunday,</strong> plan the days ahead, by hand or with AI, and Residual builds the grocery list: everything planned and not yet eaten, added up per food and sorted by aisle.</p>
      <figure class="shot"><Shot name="card-grocery" alt="The grocery list's Produce card: each food with its total weight and how many meals use it." sizes="(min-width: 40em) 35rem, 100vw" widths={[560, 1120]} /></figure>
    </div>

    <div class="stage" data-reveal>
      <p><strong>At the store,</strong> scan a barcode, or photograph the Nutrition Facts and your iPhone reads it. What you keep goes in your pantry, matched to real numbers you picked, and plans reach for it first.</p>
      <figure class="shot"><Shot name="card-pantry" alt="Pantry foods, each marked Matched · USDA with its protein, carbs and fat per 100 g, and its In stock switch on." sizes="(min-width: 40em) 35rem, 100vw" widths={[560, 1120]} /></figure>
    </div>

    <div class="stage" data-reveal>
      <p><strong>At lunch,</strong> the amounts start from the plan. Change what was different and tap Log meal. The plan stays as it was. The drift shows beside it, and a line in amber says whether it's past a band of the day.</p>
      <figure class="shot"><Shot name="card-log" alt="Lunch in Log mode: a table of plan, ate and drift. Calories 562 planned, 609 eaten, plus 47. Protein 54, 63, plus 9. In amber: Off plan, inside the day's bands." sizes="(min-width: 40em) 35rem, 100vw" widths={[560, 1120]} /></figure>
    </div>

    <div class="stage" data-reveal>
      <p><strong>On Friday,</strong> export the week for a spreadsheet, a coach or a dietitian: one row per food, what you ate beside what you planned. A meal you only planned is never reported as eaten.</p>
      <div class="csv" data-ui role="img" aria-label="Rows from an exported CSV: meal, food, eaten grams, eaten calories and planned grams for each food.">
        <div class="csv__name">Residual export.csv</div>
        <div class="csv__scroll">
          <table class="nums">
            <thead><tr>{csv[0].map((h) => <th>{h}</th>)}</tr></thead>
            <tbody>{csv.slice(1).map((r) => <tr>{r.map((c) => <td>{c}</td>)}</tr>)}</tbody>
          </table>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  /* One reading column; each paragraph opens with when it happens, and the evidence under it is exactly as wide as
     the column. */
  .week { margin-top: var(--section); }
  .week__in > * { max-width: 35rem; margin-inline: auto; }
  .week__in > h2 { margin-bottom: 3rem; }
  .stage + .stage { margin-top: 4.5rem; }
  .stage p { font-size: 1.125rem; line-height: 1.55; color: var(--label2); max-width: none; }
  .stage p strong { color: var(--text); font-weight: 600; }
  /* Cut at the card's edges, so the figure takes the card's own radius (26 points on a card 370 wide). */
  .shot { margin-top: 1.25rem; container-type: inline-size; }
  .shot :global(img) { width: 100%; height: auto; border-radius: 7.03cqw; }

  [data-ui].csv { margin-top: 1.25rem; background: var(--card); border-radius: var(--radius-row); padding: 14px 0 6px; font-size: 13px; }
  [data-ui] .csv__name { padding: 0 16px 10px; font-weight: 600; }
  [data-ui] .csv__scroll { overflow-x: auto; }
  [data-ui] table { border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; white-space: nowrap; }
  [data-ui] th, [data-ui] td { text-align: left; padding: 7px 16px; border-top: 1px solid var(--separator); }
  [data-ui] th { color: var(--label2); font-weight: 500; }
  [data-ui] td:nth-child(n+3), [data-ui] th:nth-child(n+3) { text-align: right; }

  @media (max-width: 40em) {
    .stage + .stage { margin-top: 3.5rem; }
    .stage p { font-size: 1.0625rem; }
  }
</style>
